From 3782c8384c3c2f4e3fe90ee6aff443bbf189f6a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:31:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Settings and UI for roadmap 2-6, 10-13: switches, queue
 notes, camera, catalog search, undo

Simulation switches (Settings > Simulation, all default on, each a
VMFeatures switch in FreeSO qol): smarter approach positions, avoid
unreachable objects, free will fixes, free will: count each action once
(balance), keep the queue when an object vanishes, respect
conversations.

Interface (the "Camera & Controls" tab is now "Interface"):
- Say why actions were dropped (5): a short note under the queue when an
  action disappears because it couldn't start, its object was deleted,
  or it was dropped with one (UIQueueNotices, from
  VMDiagnostics.OnActionEnded).
- Camera shortcuts (13): arrow keys pan, C centres on the selected Sim,
  F follows it, Backspace returns to the previous view, F5-F7 recall and
  Ctrl+F5-F7 save views (per lot). Ignored while typing.
- Catalog search and wheel scrolling (11): a search box in the buy
  catalog finds items of every buy category by localised name and
  description (CTSS, CatalogSearchIndex); the mouse wheel scrolls the
  catalog row instead of zooming while over it (UIWheelRouting). The
  filtered catalog list is materialised (items were read with ElementAt
  on a deferred query).
- Undo in buy and build mode (12, phase 1): Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y for buying
  (full refund via VMNetUndoBuyCmd), moving and rotating objects.
  History is per lot and cleared on returning to live mode.

Tests: room reachability and route failure memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
